  id: Sternocephalic_muscle.L
  partName: Sternocephalic muscle L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'This muscle extends from the sternum to the head and is responsible for pulling
    the head downward and to the side. It plays a key role in positioning the head
    and maintaining balance. '
  - It also assists in movements such as lowering the head. The muscle works in coordination
    with other neck muscles to provide controlled and stable head movements, supporting
    both functional and postural needs.
